            <div xml:id="d806">

                <pb facs="1122" n="994" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg994"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.632/42: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Austria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washburn</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-06-05T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 5, 1928—4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>29. Your 23, May 9, 10 a.m. Your despatch No. 1468, July 11, 1927, enclosing
                        text.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d806-f1"/> If treaty not yet signed, and if
                    agreeable to Austria, you may strike out third paragraph of Article XXV relating
                    to the termination of the sixth paragraph of Article VII. If this suppression is
                    made, strike out also first ten words of first paragraph of Article XXV.</p>
                <p>Department has altered policy toward Senate reservation to Article VII of German
                    treaty, and is signing treaty with another country including provision for the
                    national treatment of shipping, obligatory for full term of treaty. Department
                    would prefer to have all treaties submitted to the Senate the next session
                    uniform in this respect.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
